{
  "name": "deces_v1",
  "dataset": "deces",
  "description": "matchID replay v1 — 30 representative requests against the INSEE-shaped slice. Distribution: 8 advanced search, 5 block-match, 4 full-text, 3 sort, 2 function_score, 3 prefix, 3 scroll, 2 range. As of 2026-05-18, 29 entries execute against Surch HEAD and 1 entry is skipped behind gap-A3 (`bool.must_not`). B1 phase 2 (2026-05-15) lifted the 3 gap-A4 scroll skips: the runner now asserts `_scroll_id` is non-empty on every `?scroll=` request and validates `hits.total.value`; the follow-up `POST /_search/scroll` lifecycle is covered by `crates/surch-api/tests/scroll.rs`. A6 phase 2 had previously lifted the two text-typed prefix skips by adding `index_prefixes` on NOM/PRENOMS in `mapping.json` and serving them from write-time prefix postings. A6 phase 3 (2026-05-16) lifted the last skip (`prefix_date_naissance_short`, gap-A6) by adding an FST range-scan iterator on the term dictionary, exposed via `surch_index::DocumentIndex::term_prefix_doc_ids`, so keyword-typed prefix queries are answered from postings instead of falling back to source-scan. Expected hit counts and top-hit ids were captured against Surch HEAD on 2026-05-15/16 using `cargo run --release -p surch-api` + curl against the same slice; once an ES-7.x oracle replays the same slice (B1 phase 3, gated on poc-k8s), these expectations must be cross-checked.",
