    {
      "name": "prefix_date_naissance_short",
      "category": "autocomplete",
      "description": "prefix on DATE_NAISSANCE with a short input — triggered by deces-backend when `< 8` chars are typed (`queries.ts:202`, §2.4 of the intake). A6 phase 3 (2026-05-16) lifted the gap-A6 skip: matchID forbids `index_prefixes` on non-text mappings (parity with ES 7.x), so DATE_NAISSANCE (typed `keyword`) is served by an FST range scan over the term dictionary in `surch_index::TermDictionary::prefix_doc_ids`. Cost is O(matching_terms): the 1k slice spans years 1900-1960 so `194` matches 7 distinct years and 151 docs; `1962` would match 0 since the slice tops out at 1960. Expected captured against Surch HEAD on 2026-05-16.",
      "request": {
